[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: System Requirements

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: System Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The Test Case Management System (TCMS) is a declarative test case framework that converts
YAML test case definitions into executable bash scripts, captures execution results, and
verifies outcomes against expected outputs. The system supports complex test sequences with
variable capture, conditional verification, and comprehensive documentation generation for
safety-critical applications.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Verifier Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-VER-001
TITLE: Execution Log Verification
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall verify execution logs against test case definitions by comparing actual
output and exit codes with expected values.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-VER-002
TITLE: Output Matching Strategies
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support exact string matching, regex pattern matching, and JSON schema
validation for output verification.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-VER-003
TITLE: Verification Result Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall generate verification results in YAML format containing pass/fail status,
mismatch details, and step-by-step verification outcomes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-VER-004
TITLE: Batch Verification
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall verify multiple test case execution logs in sequence and aggregate results
with summary statistics.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-VER-005
TITLE: Verification Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall include verification metadata including test ID, execution timestamp,
environment information, and detailed step results in verification output.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Test Case Content Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-TC-001
TITLE: Test Case Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
Test cases shall include test_case_id, title, description, and optional tags for
organization and filtering.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-TC-002
TITLE: Test Sequences
STATEMENT: >>>
Test cases shall support multiple test sequences, each containing sequence_id, name,
and an ordered list of test steps.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-TC-003
TITLE: Test Steps
STATEMENT: >>>
Test steps shall specify description, command to execute, expected exit code, expected
output patterns, and variable capture specifications.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-TC-004
TITLE: Variable Capture
STATEMENT: >>>
Test steps shall support capturing output values using regex patterns and bash command
execution for use in subsequent steps.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-TC-005
TITLE: Expected Output Specification
STATEMENT: >>>
Expected output shall support exact string values, regex patterns, and JSON schema
validation with optional partial matching flags.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-TC-006
TITLE: Prerequisites
STATEMENT: >>>
Test cases shall support manual and automatic prerequisites with verification commands
to confirm prerequisite completion.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-TC-007
TITLE: Environment Variables
STATEMENT: >>>
Test cases shall specify required and optional environment variables with defaults and
provide substitution values in test steps.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-TC-008
TITLE: Lifecycle Hooks
STATEMENT: >>>
Test cases shall support optional hooks at script_start, setup_test, before_sequence,
after_sequence, before_step, after_step, teardown_test, and script_end execution points.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: YAML Input/Output Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-YAML-001
TITLE: YAML Schema Field
STATEMENT: >>>
All YAML test case files shall include a schema field at the root level identifying
the schema URI for validation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-YAML-002
TITLE: YAML Type Field
STATEMENT: >>>
All YAML test case files shall include a type field identifying the content type
(e.g., test-case, verification-result, container).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-YAML-003
TITLE: Test Case YAML Structure
STATEMENT: >>>
Test case YAML files shall be valid YAML with structure conforming to test-case
schema including sequences, steps, verifications, and metadata.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-YAML-004
TITLE: Execution Log JSON Output
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated execution logs shall be in JSON format with proper escaping of special
characters, newlines, and control codes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-YAML-005
TITLE: Verification Result YAML Output
STATEMENT: >>>
Verification results shall be output as YAML with structured results for each test
sequence and step.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-YAML-006
TITLE: Container YAML Format
STATEMENT: >>>
Container YAML shall aggregate multiple test results with metadata, test execution
summary, and detailed verification results.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-YAML-007
TITLE: YAML Round-trip
STATEMENT: >>>
Test case YAML files shall be loadable and deserializable to in-memory structures
without information loss.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Test Schema Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SCHEMA-001
TITLE: Test Case Schema Definition
STATEMENT: >>>
A JSON schema shall define the structure of test case YAML files including required
properties, types, constraints, and relationships.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SCHEMA-002
TITLE: Schema Validation Rules
STATEMENT: >>>
Schema shall enforce required fields (test_case_id, title, sequences), type constraints,
and value constraints (e.g., valid status values).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SCHEMA-003
TITLE: Nested Object Schemas
STATEMENT: >>>
Schema shall define nested structures for sequences, steps, verifications, prerequisites,
and environment variables with appropriate constraints.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SCHEMA-004
TITLE: Regex Pattern Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
Schema shall validate regex patterns and variable names against defined patterns to
catch syntax errors early.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SCHEMA-005
TITLE: Enum Value Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
Schema shall define allowed values for enumerated fields (status, match_type, hook_type,
on_error behavior).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SCHEMA-006
TITLE: Execution Log Schema
STATEMENT: >>>
A JSON schema shall define execution log structure including test metadata, sequence
results, step results, and exit codes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SCHEMA-007
TITLE: Verification Result Schema
STATEMENT: >>>
A JSON schema shall define verification result container structure with test data,
sequence results, and verification status.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SCHEMA-008
TITLE: Schema Validation Error Reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
Schema validation failures shall report specific field paths, constraint violations,
and expected vs. actual values.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Validator Executables

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-VAL-001
TITLE: YAML Validator (validate-yaml)
STATEMENT: >>>
The validate-yaml executable shall validate YAML test case files against JSON schema,
reporting detailed errors for schema violations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-VAL-002
TITLE: JSON Validator (validate-json)
STATEMENT: >>>
The validate-json executable shall validate JSON output files against JSON schema with
detailed constraint violation reporting.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Generator Executables

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-GEN-001
TITLE: Test Executor (test-executor)
STATEMENT: >>>
The test-executor executable shall generate bash scripts from YAML test cases and execute
them, capturing output in JSON format.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-GEN-002
TITLE: JSON Escaper (json-escape)
STATEMENT: >>>
The json-escape executable shall read text from stdin and output JSON-escaped string suitable
for inclusion in JSON documents.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-GEN-003
TITLE: JSON to YAML Converter (json-to-yaml)
STATEMENT: >>>
The json-to-yaml executable shall convert JSON input to YAML output with preserved structure
and proper formatting.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-GEN-004
TITLE: Script Cleanup Tool (script-cleanup)
STATEMENT: >>>
The script-cleanup executable shall remove generated test scripts and intermediate files
with optional preservation for debugging.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Orchestrator Executables

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-ORCH-001
TITLE: Test Orchestrator (test-orchestrator)
STATEMENT: >>>
The test-orchestrator executable shall orchestrate execution of multiple test cases,
managing sequences and aggregating results.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-ORCH-002
TITLE: Testcase Manager (testcase-manager)
STATEMENT: >>>
The testcase-manager executable shall manage test case lifecycle including creation,
validation, execution, and result reporting.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-ORCH-003
TITLE: Test Run Manager (test-run-manager / trm)
STATEMENT: >>>
The test-run-manager executable shall manage test run execution with tracking of test
status and result aggregation.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Verification and Documentation Executables

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-VER-001
TITLE: Verifier (test-verify / verifier)
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier executable shall verify execution logs against test cases and generate
verification results in YAML/JSON format.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-VER-002
TITLE: TPDG Compatibility Tool (tpdg-compat)
STATEMENT: >>>
The tpdg-compat executable shall validate container YAML compatibility with test-plan-
documentation-generator and generate reports.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Interactive Editor Executable

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-EXEC-EDT-001
TITLE: Interactive Editor (editor)
STATEMENT: >>>
The editor executable shall provide an interactive terminal UI for creating and editing
test case YAML files with real-time validation.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
